# aur.list — AUR packages, installed via the helper (paru) bootstrapped in
# phase 10. One per line; # comments and blanks ignored. Keep this short: every
# entry is a from-source build, so only put here what the official repos lack.
#
# No theme-settings GUI here (e.g. nwg-look): theme/icon/cursor/accent are owned
# end-to-end by the Quickshell Settings app (scripts/colorscheme.sh writes the
# GTK/Qt/KDE config). One place to manage everything — no extra app.
oh-my-posh-bin             # shell prompt engine; themes in dotfiles/oh-my-posh/
mpvpaper                   # video wallpapers (wallpaper.sh's video backend) — AUR-only, was
                           # wrongly in common.list where the pacman batch tripped over it
gnome-network-displays     # Cast to TV — Miracast (Samsung "Screen Mirroring", most Android TVs) AND
                           # Chromecast built-in (Google TV) from one app; captures via the
                           # xdg-desktop-portal ScreenCast (the hyprland portal), so it works outside
                           # GNOME. Needs NetworkManager + wpa_supplicant for Wi-Fi P2P (not iwd) and
                           # avahi-daemon for Chromecast discovery (phase 30). Driven by Cast.qml.
helium-browser-bin      # THE browser: Chromium-based, private, vertical tabs — themed by helium-theme.sh
mpv-uosc-git            # uosc controller for mpv — themed by colorscheme.sh (script-opts/uosc.conf)
